+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The frai-core test suite has two failing tests: (1) governance test trying to use undefined APPROVAL_STATUSES export, and (2) evaluation test expecting toxicity score of 1 but getting 0.
+
+**Approach:** Export APPROVAL_STATUSES from the governance module's index.js, and fix toxicityMetric to accept the references parameter it's passed by runEvaluations while still using default banned terms.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:** Keep all existing public exports working. Do not modify, skip, or delete any test files.
+
+**Never:** Change test logic or expectations. Do not remove any public API surface.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Import APPROVAL_STATUSES | Import from finetune/index.js | Export is available and contains ['pending', 'approved', 'rejected'] | No error |
+| Run toxicity evaluation | outputs=['Hello', 'friendly world'], no banned terms | toxicity score = 1 (all safe) | No error |
+| Run toxicity evaluation | outputs with banned terms | toxicity score < 1 | Correctly flagged |
+
+</intent-contract>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js` -- Imports APPROVAL_STATUSES from schema.js but doesn't re-export it as named export; test expects named export
