+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/governance.test.js` -- Imports APPROVAL_STATUSES as named export, fails at line 152 when trying to call join()
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` -- toxicityMetric function expects (outputs, bannedTerms) but runEvaluations calls it with (outs, refs)
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js` -- Test expects toxicity.score = 1 for clean outputs, but gets 0 because references are used as banned terms
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js` -- Add named export for APPROVAL_STATUSES at module level -- Allows test to import APPROVAL_STATUSES and call .join() on it
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` -- Update toxicityMetric signature to accept (outputs, references, bannedTerms) but only use outputs and bannedTerms -- Ensures metric works when called with references parameter from runEvaluations
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given the governance test imports APPROVAL_STATUSES, when it calls APPROVAL_STATUSES.join(', '), then it returns a string with comma-separated status values
+- Given runEvaluations calls toxicityMetric with (outs, refs), when the outputs contain no banned terms, then toxicity.score equals 1
